   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Adjectives",
     "texto": [
      "The adjective agrees with the noun. Often the feminine is formed by adding **-e**. In pairs like **grand/grande** and **petit/petite**, the final consonant, silent in the masculine, is heard when you add the -e: **grand** («grah(n)») → **grande** («grah(n)d»), **petit** («puh-TEE») → **petite** («puh-TEET»).",
      "**Jeune** and **drôle**, which already end in **-e**, have the same form in the masculine and the feminine. **Sympa** also does not change for gender, even though it ends in **-a**.",
      "With many adjectives you add **-s** in the plural, usually silent: **long → longs**.",
      "To describe: **Il est grand** (he is tall), **Elle a les cheveux longs** (she has long hair)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "From 20 to 69",
     "texto": [
      "The tens: **vingt** (20), **trente** (30), **quarante** (40), **cinquante** (50), **soixante** (60).",
      "The units are added with a hyphen: **vingt-deux**, **trente-cinq**, **soixante-neuf** (69). With one, you say **et un**: **vingt et un** (21), **trente et un** (31)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
